00:29:25,560 --> 00:29:27,837
But mine's gonna be the big one this time.

509
00:29:27,920 --> 00:29:30,100
A bright star appears, right?

510
00:29:30,960 --> 00:29:32,720
What are you excited about?

511
00:29:35,120 --> 00:29:37,997
Frankie's building us a ship and
we don't even have to pay for it?

512
00:29:38,080 --> 00:29:41,040
Right, you were asleep
when he said that. Awesome!

513
00:29:41,340 --> 00:29:43,437
I guess Frankie's not a jerk after all!

514
00:29:43,520 --> 00:29:44,697
Frankie's a nice guy!

515
00:29:44,780 --> 00:29:46,757
I can't wait to see how it turns out!

516
00:29:46,840 --> 00:29:47,670
Good.

517
00:29:47,753 --> 00:29:51,400
Now we can use the rest of our money
to buy supplies for the voyage.

518
00:29:53,840 --> 00:29:56,117
Hope this one's equipped
with a weight room.

519
00:29:56,200 --> 00:29:58,397
What happened to our 100 million berries?

520
00:29:58,480 --> 00:29:59,310
Oh, that?

521
00:29:59,393 --> 00:30:00,337
I already spent it all.

522
00:30:00,420 --> 00:30:03,537
We needed to buy lots of
meat and booze for the party.

523
00:30:03,620 --> 00:30:05,300
You spent all of my money?

524
00:30:05,580 --> 00:30:07,521
Well, everyone was really hungry.

525
00:30:10,340 --> 00:30:12,277
How could you spend so much on food?

526
00:30:12,360 --> 00:30:13,677
There's hardly anything left.

527
00:30:13,760 --> 00:30:14,677
Of course there isn't.

528
00:30:14,760 --> 00:30:16,417
The whole town was partying with us,

529
00:30:16,500 --> 00:30:18,737
and they didn't go home
until morning, remember?

530
00:30:18,820 --> 00:30:20,280
Sure was fun, huh?

531
00:30:28,060 --> 00:30:30,236
Since the ship's free, we'll be fine.

532
00:30:30,420 --> 00:30:32,020
So no worries, right?

533
00:30:32,320 --> 00:30:35,157
I just wanted nice
furniture for this ship.

534
00:30:35,240 --> 00:30:36,240
Is that so wrong?

535
00:30:36,540 --> 00:30:38,893
We can still check out the resale shops.

536
00:30:39,980 --> 00:30:42,657
Hey, can I have some of
that money to go play with?

537
00:30:42,740 --> 00:30:45,300
I'd sooner take it to the grave!

538
00:30:45,740 --> 00:30:47,940
Your allowance is revoked!

539
00:30:48,120 --> 00:30:49,780
Yes, ma 'am!

540
00:31:15,340 --> 00:31:17,337
Huh is that Usopp?

541
00:31:17,420 --> 00:31:19,517
What's that?

542
00:31:19,600 --> 00:31:20,430
Really?

543
00:31:20,513 --> 00:31:22,617
You want me to rejoin your crew?

544
00:31:22,700 --> 00:31:23,857
Do you well?

545
00:31:23,940 --> 00:31:24,817
I understand it.

546
00:31:24,900 --> 00:31:25,957
Must be rough without me.

547
00:31:26,040 --> 00:31:28,917
If I'm not around, things really
start to fall apart, don't they?

548
00:31:29,000 --> 00:31:30,237
Okay then.

549
00:31:30,320 --> 00:31:33,037
If you insist, I'll rejoin
the Straw Hat pirates.

550
00:31:33,120 --> 00:31:36,497
Yeah, that does seem to be
the best way to go about it.

551
00:31:36,580 --> 00:31:38,517
And that makes 23 scenarios.

552
00:31:38,600 --> 00:31:40,097
Hey, Chopper?

553
00:31:40,180 --> 00:31:41,657
Nice weather we're having, huh?

554
00:31:41,740 --> 00:31:42,570
Let's go.

555
00:31:43,720 --> 00:31:44,550
fishing.

556
00:31:44,633 --> 00:31:46,240
Hey, Loopy, care to join us?

557
00:31:46,600 --> 00:31:47,600
Yeah, not bad.

558
00:31:47,940 --> 00:31:49,477
And there's always the
just pretend like nothing

559
00:31:49,560 --> 00:31:51,737
happened and hop on
board the ship strategy.

560
00:31:51,820 --> 00:31:52,650
What else?

561
00:31:52,920 --> 00:31:55,617
I've decided to set out on
my own and visit Elbath.

562
00:31:55,700 --> 00:31:56,777
No, please don't go.

563
00:31:56,860 --> 00:31:58,036
We need you to stay.

564
00:31:58,200 --> 00:31:59,037
I was just kidding.

565
00:31:59,120 --> 00:32:01,437
I totally understand not wanting
to live your lives without me.

566
00:32:01,520 --> 00:32:04,060
So does that mean you're
staying? Who's up?

567
00:32:06,700 --> 00:32:07,957
Of course I will, dummies.

568
00:32:08,040 --> 00:32:12,397
Man, I didn't know anybody could love
someone as much as you guys You guys love me!

569
00:32:12,480 --> 00:32:15,060
What the hell's he doing? What an idiot.

570
00:32:21,800 --> 00:32:23,200
Hey, ice for brains.

571
00:32:23,440 --> 00:32:24,657
I know you're getting tired.

572
00:32:24,740 --> 00:32:26,017
Why don't you take a beauty nap?

573
00:32:26,100 --> 00:32:27,571
Why don't you take a nap?

574
00:32:29,480 --> 00:32:30,320
I'm beat.

575
00:32:31,540 --> 00:32:33,120
My body's burning up.

576
00:32:34,620 --> 00:32:39,960
I'm still alive, but at this
rate, I won't be for long.

577
00:32:53,660 --> 00:32:54,557
Nobody's here.

578
00:32:54,640 --> 00:32:56,640
An abandoned ship.

579
00:32:57,600 --> 00:32:58,517
Full of.

580
00:32:58,600 --> 00:33:01,220
Broken wood and scrap iron.

581
00:33:03,440 --> 00:33:04,400
Funny, huh?

582
00:33:05,220 --> 00:33:06,077
I fit right in.

583
00:33:06,160 --> 00:33:10,020
I gotta do something about
this useless body of mine!

584
00:33:10,820 --> 00:33:12,291
I'm not going to make it.

585
00:33:20,080 --> 00:33:21,500
It's finally set.

586
00:33:21,880 --> 00:33:24,821
Look, the Log Pose is
pointing to the next island.

587
00:33:24,940 --> 00:33:26,999
All that's left is to get our ship.

588
00:33:27,160 --> 00:33:28,457
This is going to be fun.

589
00:33:28,540 --> 00:33:30,277
I can't wait to see the ship myself.

590
00:33:30,360 --> 00:33:32,817
But Franky said no peeking
until he's finished.

591
00:33:32,900 --> 00:33:35,717
By the way, guys, you know
where that log is pointing?

592
00:33:35,800 --> 00:33:38,217
Might come as a big surprise
if you're not ready.

593
00:33:38,300 --> 00:33:40,065
Actually, I don't have a clue.

594
00:33:40,480 --> 00:33:44,480
Come to think of it, it kind of
looks like it's pointing down a bit.

595
00:33:44,600 --> 00:33:46,160
You bet it is!

596
00:33:46,300 --> 00:33:49,297
Because where it's pointing
is on the bottom of the ocean.

597
00:33:49,380 --> 00:33:51,120
It's called Fishman Island.

598
00:33:59,440 --> 00:34:00,270
What?

599
00:34:00,580 --> 00:34:03,940
We're finally going to
Fishman Island? Really?

600
00:34:04,520 --> 00:34:06,260
Whoa, Sanji's acting weird!

601
00:34:07,340 --> 00:34:08,660
Fishman Island, huh?

602
00:34:09,260 --> 00:34:10,090
That's tricky.

603
00:34:10,620 --> 00:34:11,720
Yeah, I guess so.

604
00:34:11,960 --> 00:34:15,607
Is that going to be tough after
what happened in your village?

605
00:34:17,320 --> 00:34:18,520
They were pirates.

606
00:34:18,740 --> 00:34:20,877
Not all fishmen are going to
give us trouble like that.

607
00:34:20,960 --> 00:34:21,790
See?

608
00:34:21,873 --> 00:34:23,657
Everybody knows Fishman Island is awesome.

609
00:34:23,740 --> 00:34:25,387
Even Zoro, and he's stupid.

610
00:34:25,820 --> 00:34:29,097
Fishman Island is one of the most
famous spots on the whole Grand Line.

611
00:34:29,180 --> 00:34:32,817
Beautiful mermaids leap and dive, painting
the water with their elegant tailpits.

612
00:34:32,900 --> 00:34:35,457
There you can frolic with the fish
and make all your dreams come true.

613
00:34:35,540 --> 00:34:37,320
Let me help, Romeo, Romeo!

614
00:34:38,240 --> 00:34:39,070
Ahem.

615
00:34:40,260 --> 00:34:41,090
Ha-ha.

616
00:34:44,040 --> 00:34:45,340
Let me dream!

617
00:34:45,560 --> 00:34:47,760
Damn it, I'm not hurting anyone!

618
00:34:48,280 --> 00:34:50,460
Relax, there's Young Mermaids, too.

619
00:34:51,240 --> 00:34:53,857
The thing is, even if the
place is nice to visit,

620
00:34:53,940 --> 00:34:56,037
that don't mean it's easy
for people to get there.

621
00:34:56,120 --> 00:34:59,197
I assume that was the case, since
it's at the bottom of the sea.

622
00:34:59,280 --> 00:35:01,520
Eh, we'll figure it out on the way.

623
00:35:01,920 --> 00:35:04,157
Well, on the way is a problem, too.

624
00:35:04,240 --> 00:35:08,997
Take a look at today's paper
and you'll understand huh?

625
00:35:09,080 --> 00:35:09,917
What is this?

626
00:35:10,000 --> 00:35:13,917
14 ships have disappeared this
month alone, all in the same place.

627
00:35:14,000 --> 00:35:15,877
I don't understand.

628
00:35:15,960 --> 00:35:19,957
They call that patch of
water the Florian Triangle.

629
00:35:20,040 --> 00:35:21,277
anyways,

630
00:35:21,360 --> 00:35:25,137
you won't be making it to Fishman Island
until after you sail through there.

631
00:35:25,220 --> 00:35:27,957
Every year,

632
00:35:28,040 --> 00:35:32,797
over 100 ships go missing in that
area and nobody has a clue as to why.

633
00:35:32,880 --> 00:35:36,717
What's spooky is that later they show up,

634
00:35:36,800 --> 00:35:39,557
totally empty, without a
single crew member in sight.

635
00:35:39,640 --> 00:35:45,117
Other people say they found ghost ships
with crews of dead men wandering the ocean,

636
00:35:45,200 --> 00:35:46,517
lost in a haze.

637
00:35:46,600 --> 00:35:48,137
You mean they're like zombies?

638
00:35:48,220 --> 00:35:52,057
Scary hanging out with a bunch
of skeletons. Sounds cool.

639
00:35:52,140 --> 00:35:56,200
Hanging out that's some
imagination you've got. No way!

640
00:35:56,400 --> 00:35:57,717
No ghost ships for us!

641
00:35:57,800 --> 00:35:58,737
Not on my watch!

642
00:35:58,820 --> 00:36:00,397
We're passing straight through that place!

643
00:36:00,480 --> 00:36:02,656
I mean, what really happens in there?

644
00:36:03,400 --> 00:36:04,320
Who knows?

645
00:36:04,760 --> 00:36:09,640
After all, nobody ever comes out of
there alive, and dead men tell no tales.

646
00:36:10,740 --> 00:36:11,720
I'd be careful.

647
00:36:12,060 --> 00:36:15,900
The water is dark, the fog
is thick, it swallows you up!

648
00:36:18,720 --> 00:36:22,400
Many a soul has been sacrificed
to that treacherous sea,

649
00:36:22,660 --> 00:36:26,357
so you better be darn ready before
you even think of setting sail.

650
00:36:26,440 --> 00:36:28,697
Although some people do
call them ghost ships,

651
00:36:28,780 --> 00:36:31,957
abandoned vessels are often
called treasure ships, too.

652
00:36:32,040 --> 00:36:35,997
We're more likely to find a ship
filled with riches than the undead.

653
00:36:36,080 --> 00:36:38,177
No, but turn down those ghost ships!

654
00:36:38,260 --> 00:36:39,789
All right, leave it to me!

655
00:36:39,920 --> 00:36:41,740
No, but I don't want it!

656
00:36:42,140 --> 00:36:44,897
I'll stock up on plenty of
food and water before we go,

657
00:36:44,980 --> 00:36:47,540
so even if we do get lost, we'll be fine.

658
00:36:47,700 --> 00:36:48,935
A treasure ship, huh?

659
00:36:49,240 --> 00:36:50,677
I wonder if they have swords.

660
00:36:50,760 --> 00:36:52,220
Hey, pirate people!

661
00:36:53,100 --> 00:36:54,140
Go ahead!

662
00:36:57,420 --> 00:36:58,700
You need something?

663
00:36:59,940 --> 00:37:01,937
Franky wants to talk to you guys.

664
00:37:02,020 --> 00:37:04,079
He's got something big to show you.

665
00:37:04,240 --> 00:37:07,537
It's been a long night, but they
finished his ship of dreams.

666
00:37:07,620 --> 00:37:09,640
And boy, is it super cool!

667
00:37:10,200 --> 00:37:11,030
Yeah!

668
00:37:11,580 --> 00:37:13,260
You mean it's done already?

669
00:37:13,500 --> 00:37:15,440
That was really fast! Of course!

670
00:37:15,740 --> 00:37:19,237
That's what happens when the best shipwrights
in the world work around the clock.

671
00:37:19,320 --> 00:37:20,397
You better believe it!

672
00:37:20,480 --> 00:37:21,377
What are we waiting for?

673
00:37:21,460 --> 00:37:22,600
Let's go! Yeah!

674
00:37:23,820 --> 00:37:24,650
Strawheads!

675
00:37:25,980 --> 00:37:27,720
We got bad news!

676
00:37:29,060 --> 00:37:30,480
Oh, hey, you guys!

677
00:37:30,940 --> 00:37:32,000
What's going on?

678
00:37:32,200 --> 00:37:33,141
They look upset.

679
00:37:33,340 --> 00:37:34,634
I wonder what's wrong.

680
00:37:39,060 --> 00:37:42,177
To be honest, we just found
out about this ourselves.

681
00:37:42,260 --> 00:37:43,697
Have you seen the wanted posters?

682
00:37:43,780 --> 00:37:44,857
Wanted posters?

683
00:37:44,940 --> 00:37:46,997
You've got a huge bounty
on your head, Straw Hat.

684
00:37:47,080 --> 00:37:49,337
They're going to hunt you down for sure.

685
00:37:49,420 --> 00:37:51,297
Actually, you've all got bounties.

686
00:37:51,380 --> 00:37:52,900
The whole crew is wanted.

687
00:37:53,420 --> 00:37:56,380
Took long enough. How much? Not me too.

688
00:37:57,060 --> 00:37:57,890
Wanted?

689
00:37:57,973 --> 00:37:59,920
No point in talking. Just look.

690
00:38:01,120 --> 00:38:03,420
Wanted posters for all seven of you.

691
00:38:07,320 --> 00:38:10,640
Straw Hat Luffy with a bounty
of 300 million berries.

692
00:38:11,820 --> 00:38:14,080
All right! It went up!

693
00:38:14,520 --> 00:38:18,380
Pirate Hunter Zoro with a
bounty of 120 million berries.

694
00:38:19,000 --> 00:38:19,830
Huh.

695
00:38:20,920 --> 00:38:24,340
Cat Burglar Nami with a
bounty of 16 million berries.

696
00:38:25,120 --> 00:38:25,950
No!

697
00:38:26,520 --> 00:38:30,500
Cotton Candy Lovin' Chopper Pet
with a bounty of 50 berries.

698
00:38:31,340 --> 00:38:32,180
50?

699
00:38:32,820 --> 00:38:36,780
Demon Child Robin with a
bounty of 80 million berries.

700
00:38:42,700 --> 00:38:43,800
Who is that?

701
00:38:44,360 --> 00:38:47,380
Black Leg Sanji, attempt
to take a photo failed.

702
00:38:47,700 --> 00:38:49,740
Bounty, 77 million berries.

703
00:38:53,340 --> 00:38:57,100
Hey, look, Sniper King
has one too, only 15.

704
00:38:57,740 --> 00:39:00,997
Well, I know that this is
probably big news for you and all.

705
00:39:01,080 --> 00:39:03,717
And I'm sure there's a lot of
pirate stuff you want to talk about.

706
00:39:03,800 --> 00:39:05,377
But, uh, hold on a sec, okay?

707
00:39:05,460 --> 00:39:08,137
I came here because I got
a favor to ask of you guys.

708
00:39:08,220 --> 00:39:09,396
Take a look at this.

709
00:39:09,760 --> 00:39:10,590
It's Franky.

710
00:39:12,080 --> 00:39:15,560
Cyborg Franky, with a bounty
of 44 million berries.

711
00:39:16,080 --> 00:39:16,940
This is awful.

712
00:39:17,040 --> 00:39:19,037
Big bro's wanted by the world government.

713
00:39:19,120 --> 00:39:20,417
What are we going to do now?

714
00:39:20,500 --> 00:39:21,997
Yeah, that's the question.

715
00:39:22,080 --> 00:39:24,737
I was happy when I found
out we didn't have bounties.

716
00:39:24,820 --> 00:39:26,467
But then this had to happen.

717
00:39:26,760 --> 00:39:29,077
Everyone in the whole
city knows about our bro.

718
00:39:29,160 --> 00:39:30,817
He can't stay in Water 7 anymore.

719
00:39:30,900 --> 00:39:32,517
And if he gets arrested again,

720
00:39:32,600 --> 00:39:35,357
I don't think we'll have the power
to save him like we did last time.

721
00:39:35,440 --> 00:39:37,277
But I'm sure he worried about us, too.

722
00:39:37,360 --> 00:39:40,917
knowing him he probably wouldn't
leave the island no matter how much

723
00:39:41,000 --> 00:39:46,017
we begged him that's why we came to
you we have no other choice we're

724
00:39:46,100 --> 00:39:49,757
begging you here Straw Hats even if
he tries to fight you gotta take our

725
00:39:49,840 --> 00:39:54,380
bro out to sea with you come on his
parents were pirates it's in his blood
